From 7e61b597166b7ec07863dd42e830e77f6d5fd6f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rou <shamay1030@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 22:26:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] security: contain malformed PIC requests and compile
 races

L-1: refuse a Link that asks for input-token logprobs at admission (run_link returns none, and the result processor asserts they exist).

L-2: validate the type and range of every pic_link field before it reaches the registry, including the recompute_mode enum; an unhashable quality_profile_id no longer raises TypeError.

L-3: track each Compile as an in-flight record (absent/compiling/resident). A conflicting same-key Compile is refused at admission, completion registers the tokens its own request was admitted with, and a Compile that cannot register (aborted, KV kept out of the radix tree, block missing) degrades to not-registered instead of raising from the batch-result loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 python/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py |  22 +-
 python/sglang/srt/pic_runtime.py        | 514 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 522 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

